WHAT IS SPEC NOISE AND WHAT IS NOT.

Clauses 3 and 6 are both stated unconditionally and collide in exactly one cell: registered,
live, `may_unregister: false`. claude-sonnet found it in review, unprompted:

  "Spec clauses 3 and 6 are both stated unconditionally and collide in this one cell ... clause
   3 says 'a registered directory produces NO steps ... appears in skipped as
   `RegisteredAndUnregisterNotPermitted`,' clause 6 says 'a directory a live run holds is
   skipped as `InUse`.'"

Mine. Now pinned -- `InUse` outranks every other skip reason, because the reason a caller most
needs is the one saying an agent is writing to it right now. Failures traceable to that cell
are vetoed.

glm's suite against sonnet fails on ordering, dedup and pair-grouping -- the three points the
SPEC CRITIQUE of this same task raised and I pinned AFTER these arms were dispatched. Vetoed
too: no arm was shown the pinned rule.

WHAT IS REAL. gemini on glm, the most serious finding of the round:

  "The root architectural flaw is calling `wtreap::disposal` directly on `wt`. In
   `wtreap::disposal`, `wt.registered` short-circuits before nameability, liveness, or
   settlement are ever inspected. By mapping `Disposal::Registered` directly to `Unregister` +
   `Delete` whenever `may_unregister` is true, the plan becomes blind to the actual state of
   the run: active runs are scheduled for deletion mid-flight."

  "There is not a single test in the suite evaluating a registered directory that is live or
   unsettled when `may_unregister` is true, completely masking the destruction of live runs."

That is the exact hazard this module exists to prevent, and glm's own fixtures hide it -- every
registered directory in them is settled and quiet. It is why glm fails gemini's clause-6 test
on more than the contested precedence.

glm on claude-sonnet, also real: sonnet files a registered directory under `Skip::Indeterminate`,
whose spec-fixed contract begins "Unregistered, not live, and no settled result" -- false of a
registered directory, so the reason reported does not describe the state.

